"""TAM Contributor Registration Consent."""

CONSENT_VERSION = '2026-11-contributor-v1'

CONSENT_TEXT = "1. Registration and Personal Information\nTAM collects my name, mobile number and email address for contributor registration, account management, communication and event administration. My account requires approval from an authorized TAM Administrator.\n\n2. Photography and Video Recording\nI will capture photographs and videos responsibly during authorized TAM events. I will respect attendees' privacy, dignity and reasonable requests not to be photographed, with particular care for children.\n\n3. Uploading Photographs and Videos\nI will upload only appropriate event-related content that I am authorized to share. I will not upload offensive, unlawful or privacy-invasive material.\n\n4. Event Media Sharing\nApproved event photographs may be viewed and downloaded by registered attendees. I understand that subsequent sharing may occur outside TAM's direct control.\n\n5. Contributor Identification and Watermarking\nTAM may display my contributor name as a watermark or attribution on photographs I upload. My identity may be associated with uploaded media in TAM's records.\n\n6. Storage and Security\nTAM uses AWS cloud services to store and process event media. Registration and activity information may be recorded for security and administration.\n\n7. Media Retention\nEvent media and registration records are handled under TAM's applicable retention and deletion practices. Different types of records may have different retention periods.\n\n8. Download and Activity Tracking\nTAM may record uploads, downloads, account identifiers, media identifiers and timestamps for administration and accountability.\n\n9. Contributor Responsibilities\nI will protect my login credentials and will not share my account. TAM Administrators may suspend or revoke contributor access for misuse.\n\n10. Photograph Deletion and Removal\nSubject to application permissions, I may request removal of photographs or delete my own uploaded photographs. TAM Administrators may remove event media when appropriate.\n\n11. Facial Recognition\nThis registration agreement does not authorize facial recognition or selfie matching. Those features require separate, explicit and optional consent.\n\n12. Consent Withdrawal and Privacy Requests\nI may contact TAM regarding my personal information or to withdraw applicable consent. Withdrawal may affect my contributor access and may not reverse downloads already completed.\n\n13. Agreement and Acceptance\nI confirm that I have read and understood this agreement and accept the responsibilities described."
